      "problem": "checkLate fails closed ('late excluded dispatch run observed; no new POST') when a run titled with any archived dispatchId appears that is not in excludedRunIds. For a dispatch retired by a no-run proof, its run id is by construction never in excludedRunIds. archivedRunIds (exact-demo-recovery.mjs:23) only collects priorRunIds and runId, and recoverExactRelease only re-verifies the current batch.exactDemoDispatches. checkLate throws before a fresh intent is saved, so exactDemoDispatches is empty at the next recovery. If such a late run ever appears, every later recovery archives nothing new, and the next ensure() fails the same way. The batch is permanently blocked except by hand-editing durable state. That is the condition the previous finding asked to remove, now in a narrower case.",
      "requested_change": "In recoverExactRelease (inside the same guarded verification), also re-inventory every archived no-run proof and excludedDispatch. If a correlated run now exists, require exactly one, with the full identity checks of validateRun, attempt 1 and status completed. Record its id in the new archive's excludedRunIds and retirementProof (for example as a lateRetiredRunIds list). Keep refusing while it is active or ambiguous. Then checkLate accepts it as an already-retired completed run.",
      "test_expectation": "A release.test or exact-demo-dispatch.test where recovery #1 first retires a no-run intent; a run with that same title later appears and the next ensure() blocks with no POST. Recovery #2 is refused while that run is in_progress. After it completes, recovery #2 adds its id to excludedRunIds and the following ensure() performs exactly one new POST. Two matching late runs keep recovery refused."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "agent-team/src/bug-pipeline/demo-deployment.mjs",
      "line": 969,
      "problem": "The delta adds run.run_attempt !== 1 to the inventory-wide check in newest(). Any deploy-backend.yml run for deploymentSha that was ever re-run (attempt>1) now makes the whole inventory PRODUCTION_PROOF_FAILED. That holds even when a newer attempt-1 workflow_dispatch run for the same SHA completed successfully. The failure is terminal and not polled. Re-running a failed production deploy after a transient Railway failure is a normal operator action. After it, the exact SHA can never be proven, and the new block hint (a manual dispatch of deploy-backend.yml may be needed) cannot help. Only a new main commit plus recovery unblocks.",
      "requested_change": "Apply the attempt==1 requirement to the selected newest run, as before. For older runs of the same SHA, accept attempt>1 only when they are completed, and still fail or pend when any run for the SHA is not completed. Alternatively, keep the strict rule but name it in the block hint (for example a distinct PRODUCTION_RUN_RERUN code saying a fresh dispatch will not help).",
      "test_expectation": "A demo-deployment.test where the inventory holds an older completed run with run_attempt 2 and a newer attempt-1 workflow_dispatch run completed/success with the deploy job successful. The proof succeeds. If the older rerun is in_progress, the result is pending or blocked, never success. The newest run with attempt>1 still fails."
